    "title": "<p>Diagnostic criteria for chronic neutrophilic leukaemia</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Volume contributors",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 703pt; background: #daeef3; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"937\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 17.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 703pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17px;\" width=\"937\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Peripheral blood WBC count &ge;&nbsp;25&nbsp;&times;&nbsp;10<sup>9</sup>/L; segmented neutrophils plus banded neutrophils constitute &ge;&nbsp;80% of the WBCs; neutrophil precursors (promyelocytes, myelocytes, and metamyelocytes) constitute &lt;&nbsp;10% of the WBCs; myeloblasts are rarely observed; monocytes constitute &lt;&nbsp;10% of the peripheral blood leukocytes; absolute monocytosis not meeting criteria for chronic mye&shy;lomonocytic leukaemia; no dysgranulopoiesis</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 17.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 703pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17px;\" width=\"937\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Hypercellular bone marrow; neutrophil granulocytes increased in percentage and number; neutrophil maturation appears normal; myeloblasts constitute &lt;&nbsp;5% of the nucleated cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 17.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 703pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17px;\" width=\"937\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Not meeting diagnostic criteria for chronic myeloid leukaemia (CML), polycythaemia vera, essential thrombocythaemia, or primary myelofibrosis, and exclusion of reactive neutrophilia</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 17.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 703pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17px;\" width=\"937\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">No evidence of disease-defining gene rearrangements such as in <em>PDGFRA</em>, <em>PDGFRB</em>, or <em>FGFR1</em>, and no <em>PCM1</em>::<em>JAK2</em> fusion</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 17.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 703pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17px;\" width=\"937\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: -11.9pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Presence of <em>CSF3R</em> p.T618I or another activating <em>CSF3R</em> mutation</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 28.05pt; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">OR</span></strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> persistent neutrophilia (&ge;&nbsp;3&nbsp;months), splenomegaly, and no identifiable cause of reactive neutrophilia including absence of a plasma cell neoplasm or, if a plasma cell neoplasm is present</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">, demonstration of clonality of myeloid cells by cytogenetic or molecular studies</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
